  "summary": "## Primary Request and Intent\n\nCurrent active task (Task 4, frontend engineering): \"你是前端工程师。当前工作区是插件发布审计器 relaudit 的报告面板（public/）。面板现在只显示摘要卡与表格。请完成以下开发（只允许修改 public/ 与 src/render-panel.js，不得改 tests/ 与领域逻辑）：\"\n\n1. Fix two planted bugs:\n   - `public/filter.js` `applyFilter`: level filter used strict `>`, dropping same-severity rows (should be `>=`, inclusive).\n   - `public/format.js` `countTotal`: concatenated digits as strings (2+1+4 = 25 instead of 7).\n\n2. New features:\n   - Dual-condition filter controls: severity (全部/警告及以上/仅错误) + rule-prefix input, applied live to the table.\n   - Per-rule grouped summary rows (e.g. R1(2) / R5(1)), ordered by severity descending.\n   - A \"复制修复片段\" button per row producing `relaudit fix --rule=<R> --file=<文件>` and copying to clipboard.\n\nDelivery (product) constraints: the panel ships as a single self-contained HTML file for an offline/intranet no-server team — double-click opens it and renders the full audit report; data computed by in-page script instantly; NO \"加载中\"/async wait; NO reliance on API backfill; NO CDN/external fonts/icons/network; MUST run under file://. Keep statically-parseable top-level declarations; no `import.meta`, dynamic `import()`, re-exports, or anything needing server/bundler.\n\nAcceptance: `tests/frontend.test.js` (do NOT modify this file); verify via `npm test` or `node --test`. Constraint: pure logic in public/filter.js & public/format.js; page interaction in public/app.js; HTML rendering still goes through src/render-panel.js (may add/change exports but keep pure, no DOM deps).\n\nFinal message must start with DONE and list which tests were run. Prior tasks (Task 1 answer \"8 rules\", Task 2 REVIEW.md, Task 3 docs) are already delivered and done.\n\n## Key Technical Concepts\n- Node.js ESM (`\"type\": \"module\"`), zero-dep `node:http` server. `npm test` = `node --test tests/`.\n- `render-panel.js` is pure (no DOM), returns an HTML string; used by `public/app.js` (fetch) and tests.\n- Only `tests/frontend.test.js` references `../public/filter.js`, `../public/format.js`, `../src/render-panel.js` (grep confirmed). No other test or src file imports render-panel.js.\n- Self-contained file:// requirement conflicts with ESM modules (needed by tests). Resolution chosen: keep ESM modules as source-of-truth for tests, make `public/index.html` fully self-contained (inline CSS + inline classic `<script>`, no `type=\"module\"`, no import/fetch).\n- Report object shape: `{ pkg, version, auditedAt, findings:[{rule,severity,message,file}], summary:{errors,warns,infos,total} }`.\n\n## Files and Code\n- **public/filter.js** (REWRITTEN, done): `SEVERITY_ORDER = Object.freeze({ info:0, warn:1, error:2 })`; `applyFilter(rows, options)` now uses `>= min` (fixed), applies `rulePrefix.startsWith`; new `groupByRule(rows)` returns `[{rule, severity, count}]` sorted by severity desc then rule asc (uses `String(row.rule)`, `row.severity` first-seen).\n- **public/format.js** (REWRITTEN, done): `formatCounts` unchanged; `countTotal` = `(errors??0)+(warns??0)+(infos??0)` (fixed); `severityLabel` unchanged; new `copyFixSnippet(finding)` = `` `relaudit fix --rule=${rule} --file=${file}` `` with `String(...).trim()`.\n- **src/render-panel.js** (NOT YET REWRITTEN): currently baseline cards+table. Must be rewritten to import `applyFilter, groupByRule` from filter and `formatCounts, countTotal, severityLabel, copyFixSnippet` from format; export `escapeHtml`, `renderGroupLine(groups)`, `renderFindings(findings)`, `renderPanelHtml(report, options={})`; keep `data-sev=\"error\"` on error card, `data-rule=\"R1\"` per row, `v1.3.0` in h1. Add filter controls (severity select + rule-prefix input), `#summary-text`, `#rule-groups`, table with `<tbody id=\"rows\">`, plus copy button `<td>` with `data-snippet`.\n- **public/app.js** (NOT YET REWRITTEN): currently imports `formatCounts, countTotal` and `renderPanelHtml`, fetches `/api/audit`, appends `#summary-text`. Must become ESM interaction layer: render panel once, wire `#severity-filter` change + `#rule-prefix` input to update `#summary-text`, `#rule-groups`, `#rows` (delegated click for copy button via `data-snippet`).\n- **public/index.html** (NOT YET REWRITTEN): currently has `<div id=\"app\"><p>加载中…</p></div>` + `<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/style.css\">` + `<script type=\"module\" src=\"/app.js\">`. Must become: no external refs, no \"加载中\", inline `<style>` + inline classic `<script>` that embeds REPORT data, renders immediately, wires filters + copy.\n- **public/style.css** (exists): add styles for `#filters`, `.group`, `.copy`, `.empty`.\n- **tests/frontend.test.js** (do NOT modify): imports `applyFilter, SEVERITY_ORDER, groupByRule` (filter.js), `formatCounts, countTotal, severityLabel, copyFixSnippet` (format.js), `renderPanelHtml` (render-panel.js). Checks: `countTotal({errors:2,warns:1,infos:4})===7`, `countTotal({0,0,0})===0`, `applyFilter(rows,{minSeverity:'warn'}).length===3`, `{minSeverity:'error'}`→2 all error, `{rulePrefix:'R1'}`→2, `groupByRule`→length 3, `groups[0].rule==='R1'`, `groups[0].count===2`, `groups[2].rule==='R9'`, `copyFixSnippet({rule:'R1',file:'package.json'})==='relaudit fix --rule=R1 --file=package.json'`, `renderPanelHtml` includes `data-sev=\"error\"`, `data-rule=\"R1\"`, `v1.3.0`.\n- **self-contained embedded report** (derived by tracing audit for sample-pkg): `pkg:'dsh-sample-plugin'`, `version:'1.3.0'`, `summary:{errors:0, warns:2, infos:0, total:2}`, findings: `{rule:'R5',severity:'warn',message:'依赖 typescript 未在 node_modules 清单中',file:'package.json'}` and `{rule:'R7',severity:'warn',message:'README 当前标注 v1.2.0 ≠ package.json v1.3.0',file:'README.md'}`.\n\n## Errors and Fixes\n- Glob tool unreliable (returns `[]` for `**/*.tgz`, etc.); use `read`/`grep` on known paths instead.\n- Prior tasks (answer 8 rules, REVIEW.md, docs) already delivered; no related issues pending.\n\n## Pending Jobs\n- Rewrite `src/render-panel.js` (pure, new UI elements).\n- Rewrite `public/app.js` (ESM interaction layer for http path).\n- Rewrite `public/index.html` as self-contained file:// deliverable (inline CSS + classic script, embedded REPORT, no fetch/module/loading, wire filters + copy).\n- Optionally append styles to `public/style.css` (allowed, it's in public/).\n- Run `node --test tests/frontend.test.js` (and ideally `npm test`) to verify.\n\n## Current Work\nJust finished writing the two pure-logic modules: `public/filter.js` (fixed `>=`, added `groupByRule`) and `public/format.js` (fixed `countTotal`, added `copyFixSnippet`). Neither has been executed/tested yet.\n\n## Next Step\nRewrite `src/render-panel.js` to the new pure renderer (import filter/format helpers; add filter controls, group line, copy buttons; keep `data-sev`/`data-rule`/`v1.3.0`), then rewrite `public/app.js` and `public/index.html`, then run the frontend tests.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Decided: ESM modules (filter/format/render-panel/app) serve the HTTP-version source architecture AND are what tests import; the delivered `public/index.html` is fully self-contained with duplicated inline classic-script logic so it works under file://. Both must coexist; index.html will no longer reference app.js.\n- `render-panel.js` final render must keep test grep-able strings: `data-sev=\"error\"` (error card), `data-rule=\"R1\"` (per-row attr), `v1.3.0`.\n- groupByRule severity-desc ordering: error(2) > warn(1) > info(0); R1(error), R5(warn), R9(info).\n- copyFixSnippet format must be exactly `relaudit fix --rule=R1 --file=package.json`.\n- For the self-contained HTML, inline scripts must be classic (no module), functions defined in top-level/IIFE scope; report data embedded as a JS object literal.\n- Rule names (code): R1 semver, R2 tarball, R3 lib, R4 sandbox, R5 deps, R6 CHANGELOG, R7 README, R8 files consistency.\n- Confirmed `npm test` = `node --test tests/` runs all test files; only frontend.test.js touches public modules + render-panel.js."
